IMPORT prelude

-- Evidence (Civil Proceedings in Other Jurisdictions) Act 1979 (Singapore) -- when the General Division of the High Court may help a
-- foreign court obtain evidence in Singapore (ss 2, 3), what its order may and may not require of a person (s 4), and when a person
-- may refuse to give the evidence, and whether evidence given under protest is sent abroad (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/ECPOJA1979.txt. The deposit says the revised edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the body is Act 40 of 2019 ([40/2019], the General Division renaming). The deposit's metadata records it as
-- the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. It is requirement REQ-0047: tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life relevance. The
-- requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet. The
-- Act is six sections long, so the whole of its operative part is encoded. Not encoded: s 1 (short title), s 6 (the Rules
-- Committee's power to make Rules of Court on the manner of applications and references), the court's discretion under s 4(1) as to
-- what is "appropriate", and the amount of any witness allowance (the Act borrows it from High Court practice and states no figure).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Evidence (Civil Proceedings in Other Jurisdictions) Act 1979 -- assistance to foreign courts`

§§ `2 and 3 -- when the High Court has the powers`

-- s 2: "civil proceedings", in relation to the requesting court, means "proceedings in any civil or commercial matter but does not
-- include proceedings arising out of any fiscal, monetary or revenue law or measure". "request" includes "any commission, order or
-- other process issued by or on behalf of the requesting court".
-- s 3: where an application is made to the General Division of the High Court "for an order for evidence to be obtained in Singapore"
-- and the Court is satisfied that (a) the application is made "pursuant to a request issued by or on behalf of a court or tribunal
-- ... exercising jurisdiction in a country or territory outside Singapore"; and (b) the evidence is "to be obtained for the purposes
-- of civil proceedings which either have been instituted before the requesting court or whose institution before that court is
-- contemplated", the Court "has the powers conferred on it by this Act".
-- (Whether the application is made by a party, the foreign court or someone else, the Act does not say; s 6 leaves the manner of
-- application to Rules of Court.)
DECLARE Application HAS
    `made to the General Division of the High Court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `seeks evidence to be obtained in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made pursuant to a request by or on behalf of a court or tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the requesting court sits outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the matter is civil or commercial` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal, monetary or revenue law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the proceedings are instituted or contemplated` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign proceedings are civil proceedings` IF
        `the application`'s `the matter is civil or commercial`
    AND (NOT `the application`'s `the proceedings arise out of a fiscal, monetary or revenue law`)

GIVEN `the application` IS AN Application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the High Court has the powers under the Act` IF
        `the application`'s `made to the General Division of the High Court`
    AND `the application`'s `seeks evidence to be obtained in Singapore`
    AND `the application`'s `made pursuant to a request by or on behalf of a court or tribunal`
    AND `the application`'s `the requesting court sits outside Singapore`
    AND `the foreign proceedings are civil proceedings` `the application`
    AND `the application`'s `the proceedings are instituted or contemplated`

§§ `4 -- what an order may require`

-- s 4(1): the Court may "by order ... make such provision for obtaining evidence in Singapore as may appear ... to be appropriate for
-- the purpose of giving effect to the request", and the order "may require a person specified in the order to take such steps as the
-- [Court] may consider appropriate".
-- (2): in particular (a) "the examination of witnesses, either orally or in writing"; (b) "the production of documents"; (c) "the
-- inspection, photographing, preservation, custody or detention of any property"; (d) "the taking of samples of any property and the
-- carrying out of any experiments on or with any property"; (e) "the medical examination of any person"; (f) "the taking and testing
-- of samples of blood from any person".
-- (3): an order "must not require any particular steps to be taken unless they are steps which can be required to be taken by way of
-- obtaining evidence for the purposes of civil proceedings in the General Division of the High Court" -- but this "does not preclude
-- the making of an order requiring a person to give testimony (either orally or in writing) otherwise than on oath where this is asked
-- for by the requesting court".
-- (4): an order "shall not require a person -- (a) to state what documents relevant to the proceedings ... are or have been in the
-- person's possession, custody or power; or (b) to produce any documents other than particular documents specified in the order as
-- being documents appearing to the [Court] to be, or to be likely to be, in the person's possession, custody or power".
-- Every paragraph in (2) is "subject to this section", so (3) governs it: a step listed in (2) still needs to be one a Singapore civil
-- court could require.
DECLARE Step IS ONE OF
    `examining a witness orally or in writing`
    `producing particular documents specified in the order`
    `producing documents not specified in the order`
    `stating what relevant documents the person has or had`
    `inspecting, photographing or detaining property`
    `taking samples of property or experimenting on it`
    `a medical examination`
    `taking and testing blood samples`
    `giving testimony otherwise than on oath`
    `another step to give effect to the request`

GIVEN `the step` IS A Step,
      `requirable in Singapore High Court civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the requesting court asked for unsworn testimony` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the documents appear likely to be in the person's possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order may require the step` IF
    CONSIDER `the step`
    WHEN `stating what relevant documents the person has or had` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `producing documents not specified in the order` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `producing particular documents specified in the order` THEN
            `requirable in Singapore High Court civil proceedings`
        AND `the documents appear likely to be in the person's possession`
    WHEN `giving testimony otherwise than on oath` THEN
            `requirable in Singapore High Court civil proceedings`
        OR  `the requesting court asked for unsworn testimony`
    OTHERWISE `requirable in Singapore High Court civil proceedings`

-- s 4(5): a person "required to attend at any place" by an order "is entitled to the like payment for expenses and loss of time as on
-- attendance as a witness in civil proceedings before the General Division of the High Court". The figure is an input: the Act states
-- none.
GIVEN `required to attend by the order` IS A BOOLEAN, `the High Court witness allowance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the payment due for attending` MEANS
    IF `required to attend by the order` THEN `the High Court witness allowance` ELSE 0

§§ `5 -- privilege of witnesses`

-- s 5(1): a person "is not compelled" by an order under s 4 to give any evidence "which the person could not be compelled to give --
-- (a) in civil proceedings in the General Division of the High Court in Singapore; or (b) subject to subsection (2), in civil
-- proceedings in the country or territory in which the requesting court exercises jurisdiction".
-- (2): (1)(b) "does not apply unless the claim ... is either -- (a) supported by a statement contained in the request (whether ...
-- unconditionally or subject to conditions that are fulfilled); or (b) conceded by the applicant for the order"; where it is not, the
-- person "may ... be required to give the evidence ... but that evidence is not to be transmitted to the requesting court if that
-- court, on the matter being referred to it, upholds the claim".
-- (3): nor is a person compelled to give evidence "if the person's doing so would be prejudicial to the security of Singapore", and a
-- Minister's certificate to that effect "is conclusive evidence of that fact".
-- (4): "giving evidence" includes "answering any question and ... producing any document".
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `privileged in Singapore civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `privileged in the requesting country's civil proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign privilege is supported by a statement in the request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `any conditions on that statement are fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the foreign privilege is conceded by the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `giving it would prejudice the security of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has certified prejudice to security` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the foreign privilege is recognised here` IF
        `the claim`'s `privileged in the requesting country's civil proceedings`
    AND (    (`the claim`'s `the foreign privilege is supported by a statement in the request`
              AND `the claim`'s `any conditions on that statement are fulfilled`)
         OR  `the claim`'s `the foreign privilege is conceded by the applicant`)

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the security exemption applies` IF
        `the claim`'s `giving it would prejudice the security of Singapore`
    OR  `the claim`'s `the Minister has certified prejudice to security`

GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person can be compelled to give the evidence` IF
        (NOT `the claim`'s `privileged in Singapore civil proceedings`)
    AND (NOT `the foreign privilege is recognised here` `the claim`)
    AND (NOT `the security exemption applies` `the claim`)

-- s 5(2), second limb: evidence given over an unsupported, unconceded foreign claim is held back if the requesting court, on a
-- reference, upholds the claim. Where no such claim was made, nothing in s 5 holds the evidence back.
GIVEN `the claim` IS A Claim, `the requesting court upholds the claim on reference` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the evidence may be transmitted to the requesting court` IF
    IF      `the claim`'s `privileged in the requesting country's civil proceedings`
        AND (NOT `the foreign privilege is recognised here` `the claim`)
    THEN NOT `the requesting court upholds the claim on reference`
    ELSE TRUE
